# CODEOWNERS: trust boundaries only (ISS-259 supply chain hardening, narrowed 2026-10-05)
#
# A path is owned here when a bad change to it could leak a credential, widen
# what an agent or the public internet can reach, or change which code or image
# runs with privileges. Ordinary code is NOT owned: it is gated by the
# workflow's independent verification, codex review and CI. Owning ordinary
# code queued safe changes behind a human (8 PRs on 2026-10-04).
#
# Adding a path: name the boundary it protects. Own the CODE that enforces a
# boundary, not only its settings, or the check can be removed around them.

# --- CI/CD and this file: code execution in CI, release credentials, publish
# rights. Agents cannot push here at all (#1024).
